From: Infinity Mods <noreply@infinitymods.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Show the other players' neon through the Infinity hook's car-state sync

Under Infinity, in an online free-roam world, the Infinity hook (azimuth-tls.dll, or ExtraOptions.Infinity's
winmm.dll) exports InfinityCarSync_* (ABI version 1; CR-L53, OD-248). Underglow finds it with GetProcAddress
only and registers as sync id 1. It hands the hook the local car's look (on/off, the lit parts, LED level,
colors as RGB, effects, brightness, speed, the shape) as one 40-byte blob whenever it changes, and an "off"
blob as soon as it registers (never nothing: the world forwards other players' blobs only to a hook that
sends one). It asks the hook about every car but the player's (the kind doesn't tell a player's car apart:
2 or 5 in a hosted world, 3 in an official one); on the ones the hook matched to another player it shows their neon:
the 8 nearest within 150 m, at most 32 lights each, from the one shared light manager (at most 256 extra
beam presets). An audio effect on another player's car is a steady glow. Lights of a car that leaves,
whose blob is gone or when the sync stops go dark and are reused. Without the hook, or with another
version of its API, nothing of this runs. The local car's neon is unchanged.
The API's header, src/infinity_carsync.h, is the Infinity hook's own (MIT), vendored as it is.
---
